WEBVTT

00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:55.230
I can't save anyone.

00:01:56.360 --> 00:02:01.820
If I can't save them I'll at least record their deaths explicitly.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:08.120
I will collect all deaths.

00:02:35.230 --> 00:02:39.110
Murder Speculation Part A
September, 1995

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:40.860
Excuse me!

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:51.710
I knew it was you!

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:59.260
Who are... you?

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.850
You're looking cool as usual,

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:10.180
Shiki.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:12.190
Not really.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:14.650
Like I said, there was a murder...

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:17.650
on the last day of the summer break.

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:20.400
It's not that it has nothing to do with me.

00:03:26.660 --> 00:03:27.910
I have an umbrella.

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:35.750
We had a farewell party for an upperclassman

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.840
by the name of Rio Shirazumi.

00:04:03.070 --> 00:04:07.620
Kokutou, do you understand that I am a psycho?

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.750
Unfortunately...

00:04:14.460 --> 00:04:16.460
I'm a murderer.

00:04:28.100 --> 00:04:32.770
Shiki's definition of murder... is to kill me.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:39.980
She kills those who try to release me.

00:04:41.190 --> 00:04:44.030
Shiki wants to kill everyone who tries to open the lid of her...

00:04:44.150 --> 00:04:48.530
in order to protect herself.

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:56.080
If this goes on like this, I'm positive I'll kill you.

00:04:59.170 --> 00:05:01.750
Because I didn't see it.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:06.800
You just happened to be there and that's all I saw.

00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.890
So, I decided to believe...

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:44.300
What an idiotic optimist!

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.800
You can't do anything like that. I know that for sure!

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.760
What do you know for sure?

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.230
What can you understand about me?

00:05:58.980 --> 00:06:02.150
What can you believe about me?

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.780
I have no foundation,

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:09.240
but I think I'll continue to believe in you.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:12.660
Yeah. Because I love you.

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.290
I want to keep believing in you.

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:43.980
Kokutou...

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.360
Kokutou!!

00:06:59.460 --> 00:07:02.790
I want to kill you.

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:15.640
I think I wander about in a peopleless town because I want to be alone.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:22.600
Or, do I do it because I want to believe I'm alone?

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:28.530
The Hollow Shrine
June, 1998

00:08:11.070 --> 00:08:14.280
There was no... end...

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.720
So, this is... death...

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:05.290
No...

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.100
She's empty.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:26.180
It's insufficient, like a hole.

00:09:26.270 --> 00:09:30.980
But, no matter how much she herself can't feel it,

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.690
she is still Shiki Ryougi.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:36.740
You...

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:38.030
Yes?

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.120
You're not a doctor, are you?

00:09:41.530 --> 00:09:44.120
Right. I'm a magus by profession.

00:09:46.750 --> 00:09:50.880
But... did SHIKI really die in vain, Shiki Ryougi?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:52.090
I will... enter...

00:09:57.630 --> 00:09:58.970
I don't care.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.300
If "that" wants to fill me,

00:10:02.430 --> 00:10:03.930
that's fine by me.

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:22.320
In short, an empty hole must be filled with something.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:23.830
Not with memories.

00:10:23.910 --> 00:10:28.000
She'll have to create a newly assembled self.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:32.290
It's hollow and no one can help her.

00:10:54.980 --> 00:10:56.230
Don't hesitate!

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:07.490
That's a "living" corpse, isn't it? If so...

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:11.960
Whatever it is, I'll kill it for sure!

00:11:22.010 --> 00:11:23.130
Out of my way!

00:11:29.060 --> 00:11:31.140
You lump of death!

00:11:31.730 --> 00:11:33.900
Don't stand in front of me!

00:12:05.090 --> 00:12:06.760
I won't let you get away...

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:10.010
I will kill my weak self!

00:12:11.430 --> 00:12:15.190
I will not allow you to have Shiki Ryougi!

00:12:46.300 --> 00:12:49.140
He disappeared in exchange for... what?

00:12:49.510 --> 00:12:52.140
In order to protect... what?

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.440
SHIKI... he's gone.

00:12:55.690 --> 00:13:03.320
It was probably his dream... his dream of living a happy life,

00:13:04.110 --> 00:13:08.570
though he's left me with such deep loneliness...

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.760
Do you know who I am?

00:13:31.720 --> 00:13:34.220
Yeah... I knew...

00:13:35.270 --> 00:13:38.770
I knew that you were the only one waiting for me

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:44.650
and you were the only one protecting me...

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.530
Mikiya Kokutou...

00:13:53.240 --> 00:13:55.290
sounds like a French poet's name.

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:01.670
I'm glad it cleared up...

00:14:04.710 --> 00:14:06.800
It's perfect for leaving the hospital.

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:15.810
Yeah... So, there's something that won't disappear...

00:14:26.360 --> 00:14:29.240
Let's compare the human brain to a TV.

00:14:29.360 --> 00:14:33.450
Both your brain and mine have a lot of different channels,

00:14:33.660 --> 00:14:39.160
but they're always fixated on the most-watched channel of all... Channel 8.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:42.580
In other words, they only have eyes for the program called Common Sense.

00:14:42.710 --> 00:14:47.170
Because that's the easiest way to lead a peaceful life.

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:49.880
Those who are called psychics...

00:14:49.970 --> 00:14:53.010
...live beyond the scope of such common sense.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:56.600
For example, by turning on Channel 4,

00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:59.600
let's say you were able to move objects telekinetically.

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:02.270
But in doing so you would never glimpse Common Sense

00:15:02.350 --> 00:15:04.190
on Channel 8, would you?

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:07.110
Your very existence would be an anomaly.

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:10.950
Which is why we refer to such psychics as follows:

00:15:11.280 --> 00:15:13.660
Unfit existences.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:19.160
From what I've heard, the unfit existence that appears in your story

00:15:19.910 --> 00:15:23.370
possesses such tremendous power of distortion that she can twist off a person's arm,

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.540
rotating them at will, either to the left or right.

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:29.760
It is unprecedented for anyone to possess two channels...

00:15:29.840 --> 00:15:31.300
...and use them simultaneously.

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:35.720
Or should we assume that there are actually more than two channels?

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:39.640
Listen, if there really is an unfit existence like that at large,

00:15:39.730 --> 00:15:41.560
perhaps you shouldn't have anything to do with it.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:44.060
What's that?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:47.230
How can you turn an unfit existence into a fit existence?

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:50.400
You'd probably have to kill it.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:53.660
After all, destroying abnormal channels is the same

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:55.820
as demolishing the brain.

00:15:56.160 --> 00:15:58.160
As yet, there's no convenient way to destroy the brain

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:02.250
without also wiping out all bodily functions.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.380
That in itself would be a supernatural power!

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.710
Channel 12 or so, if you will.

00:16:11.340 --> 00:16:15.510
These beings are already unfit as far as existing goes.

00:16:15.720 --> 00:16:17.850
They shouldn't exist at all.

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:18.850
Or rather...

00:16:18.930 --> 00:16:20.640
They can't bear to exist.

00:16:24.980 --> 00:16:28.940
Twist!!!

00:16:30.730 --> 00:16:32.440
I'm sorry...

00:16:33.110 --> 00:16:37.240
but I need to do this.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:42.750
This is the only way I can be like others.

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:50.420
Remaining Sense of Pain
July, 1998

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.590
We finally meet, Asagami.

00:16:52.880 --> 00:16:55.260
Shiki... Ryougi...

00:16:57.930 --> 00:17:00.470
I'm going to kill the present you.

00:17:04.270 --> 00:17:09.310
I didn't want anyone to know I couldn't feel pain.

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:15.570
Others need to think I'm normal, or else it's over for me...

00:17:19.910 --> 00:17:22.240
I must kill you.

00:17:26.790 --> 00:17:30.840
I really don't want to kill people.

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:39.180
I'm not sure about that.

00:17:40.720 --> 00:17:42.140
Shiki...?

00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:44.600
We are alike.

00:17:47.940 --> 00:17:48.940
Don't mess with me!

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:58.490
I can finally feel pain... I finally feel alive...

00:18:10.330 --> 00:18:11.170
Fujino,

00:18:11.630 --> 00:18:14.800
once the wound heals, it won't hurt any more.

00:18:17.800 --> 00:18:21.300
I didn't understand what she said,

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:25.970
...because I had never felt pain.

00:18:32.480 --> 00:18:33.480
Shiki!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:37.650
Souren Araya

00:18:38.070 --> 00:18:42.070
It's a pain in the ass, so take care of it before Kokutou returns.

00:18:46.330 --> 00:18:47.790
By the way, Miss Touko...

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.750
I found out that Fujino Asagami was insensitive to pain...

00:18:49.830 --> 00:18:51.830
just as I had thought.

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.040
But she used to be completely normal.

00:18:55.460 --> 00:18:56.250
What did you say?

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:01.090
It probably started out as a minor misunderstanding.

00:19:02.680 --> 00:19:03.550
Shiki is right.

00:19:03.850 --> 00:19:06.140
It's too late for Fujino Asagami.

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:12.850
We finally meet, Asagami.

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.190
Shiki... Ryougi...

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:21.150
You are a beast that knows the taste of blood.

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.200
No, that's you.

00:19:40.220 --> 00:19:42.380
You're totally out of control.

00:20:00.360 --> 00:20:01.320
Twist.

00:20:09.540 --> 00:20:11.330
Twist!

00:20:22.760 --> 00:20:26.050
Twist!!!

00:20:32.940 --> 00:20:42.280
It hurts! It hurts!

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.780
It hurts!

00:20:54.920 --> 00:20:57.170
If it hurts...

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.960
you should've said so.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.680
I sympathize with her.

00:21:12.640 --> 00:21:16.310
The wound in her heart will keep hurting.

00:21:16.810 --> 00:21:18.690
That pains me.

00:21:25.360 --> 00:21:28.780
You're too soft-hearted. Besides...

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:34.450
I don't have fancy stuff like "good sense".

00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:38.290
Do you think someone like that should be left alone?

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.840
I see. I've got no choice.

00:21:41.960 --> 00:21:45.210
I'll carry your sin in your place.

00:21:47.050 --> 00:21:49.340
I've just remembered...

00:21:49.590 --> 00:21:53.510
you've always joked like that with a straight face.

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:54.930
Honestly...

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:57.730
Shiki didn't do well with that kind of stuff.

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.270
All right.

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:04.320
I think I'm strong enough to carry one girl.

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:10.360
One more confession...

00:22:10.700 --> 00:22:13.870
I think I carried a sin this time.

00:22:14.330 --> 00:22:18.460
But, in exchange, I learned what I wanted.

00:22:18.870 --> 00:22:24.960
It's vague and risky, but I have to hold on to it.

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:30.130
But that thing wasn't as bad as I'd thought.

00:22:30.220 --> 00:22:33.350
That makes me a little happy... just a little...

00:22:34.260 --> 00:22:39.060
A little murderous impulse toward you...

00:22:48.900 --> 00:22:55.080
Thinking back, that was the first truly happy smile she showed me

00:22:55.620 --> 00:22:57.660
since she woke up.

00:23:14.010 --> 00:23:17.100
Overlooking View
September, 1998

00:23:34.530 --> 00:23:37.370
Just when is he coming back to us?

00:23:37.450 --> 00:23:39.080
That boy of ours?

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:03.310
Can you fly?

00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:14.660
You just...

00:24:14.780 --> 00:24:16.620
...don't get it!

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:21.500
...fall...

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:22.910
Fall... Fall...

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:24.000
Fall...

00:24:24.080 --> 00:24:26.880
Fall, fall, fall!

00:24:36.180 --> 00:24:37.470
Good morning, Shiki.

00:24:42.850 --> 00:24:45.390
After all, you're Shiki.

00:24:52.110 --> 00:24:53.780
You fall.

00:25:00.490 --> 00:25:01.870
I wanted...

00:25:06.830 --> 00:25:08.920
him to take me with him...

00:25:22.100 --> 00:25:27.230
...I think I should end it by falling to my death from an overlooking view.

00:25:32.230 --> 00:25:33.110
You are...?

00:25:33.570 --> 00:25:36.400
A magus, Souren Araya,

00:25:36.490 --> 00:25:38.570
He Who Kills Shiki.

00:25:39.070 --> 00:25:41.330
Why are you trying to kill me?

00:25:42.240 --> 00:25:46.830
Neither Kirie Fujou or Fujino Asagami were effective.

00:25:47.170 --> 00:25:47.710
What?!

00:25:48.170 --> 00:25:53.800
She chose death and you chose life in the face of death.

00:25:54.340 --> 00:26:00.340
She enjoyed murder, annihilating life, while you respectfully performed killing.

00:26:01.100 --> 00:26:03.140
You probably know by now...

00:26:03.270 --> 00:26:10.020
that they are your fellows and killers completely opposite from Shiki Ryougi.

00:26:10.360 --> 00:26:15.030
I've prepared them just for you to offer as sacrifices.

00:26:15.190 --> 00:26:16.610
Why you...

00:26:18.240 --> 00:26:25.120
Shiki Ryougi. "Nil" is the very source of your chaos impulse.

00:26:25.950 --> 00:26:31.830
Face your darkness and call up your name.

00:26:33.590 --> 00:26:34.630
Isn't this yours?

00:26:40.300 --> 00:26:42.680
Paradox Paradigm.
November, 1998

00:26:43.140 --> 00:26:44.810
I'm Tomoe Enjou.

00:26:45.520 --> 00:26:47.310
Shiki Ryougi.

00:26:49.140 --> 00:26:50.810
You have no place to sleep, right?

00:26:51.310 --> 00:26:53.400
Use this place for a while.

00:26:57.070 --> 00:26:59.860
You said you didn't' have a key last night.

00:27:00.200 --> 00:27:01.660
I replaced it with a new one.

00:27:02.070 --> 00:27:03.570
I told you I didn't need it.

00:27:03.950 --> 00:27:07.830
A home without a lock is not a home.

00:27:20.180 --> 00:27:21.840
Will you die for me?

00:27:45.200 --> 00:27:47.530
This is a simple experiment.

00:27:47.950 --> 00:27:51.290
All these people were dysfunctional to begin with.

00:27:51.370 --> 00:27:55.670
They all killed each other within a short month.

00:27:56.800 --> 00:28:03.930
Enjou, it looks like the residents' last day is being repeated in this building.

00:28:04.220 --> 00:28:05.720
The day of death...

00:28:05.930 --> 00:28:12.600
The Ogawa Condo is the embodiment of the Yin-Yang symbol, duality within one.

00:28:40.590 --> 00:28:41.760
You're the main cause!

00:28:43.090 --> 00:28:45.630
FUGU... KONGOU... DAKATSU...

00:28:54.850 --> 00:28:56.650
You'll get lost in the netherworld.

00:28:57.020 --> 00:28:58.520
Hello, Aozaki.

00:28:59.190 --> 00:29:04.990
There is a purpose. The ultimate goal for magi is... The Radix.

00:29:05.110 --> 00:29:10.620
Either way, the endless goal and a colony that will never be rewarded...

00:29:10.910 --> 00:29:12.790
the world calls them magi.

00:29:12.950 --> 00:29:15.790
Death lines are frays of objects.

00:29:15.870 --> 00:29:21.420
Being able to see them means understanding the truth about the objects, which means...

00:29:24.630 --> 00:29:27.340
Everything is recorded in the radix.

00:29:27.720 --> 00:29:31.810
Shiki might be having a dream in the Supreme Ultimate.

00:29:41.230 --> 00:29:43.150
You're a good boy, Tomoe.

00:29:43.440 --> 00:29:45.650
The key is the proof that we are a family.

00:29:48.570 --> 00:29:50.530
This head is still alive.

00:29:52.740 --> 00:29:54.580
You're just a fake puppet.

00:29:54.660 --> 00:29:57.000
Give me a break!

00:30:03.670 --> 00:30:05.590
I loved Ryougi!

00:30:06.130 --> 00:30:08.050
My feelings are real!

00:30:11.600 --> 00:30:14.310
I existed here...

00:30:40.880 --> 00:30:42.000
SHUKU!

00:32:18.560 --> 00:32:23.310
Now you look like a girl your age.

00:32:24.940 --> 00:32:27.980
Your bound field saved Shiki.

00:32:28.520 --> 00:32:30.690
You failed again this time.

00:32:32.490 --> 00:32:35.360
Why do you run yourself into ground?

00:32:36.910 --> 00:32:41.830
Why do you so desperately seek the Vortex of Radix?

00:32:43.330 --> 00:32:46.330
Humans are hopeless.

00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:49.840
It's so long ago...

00:32:50.460 --> 00:32:53.670
You can't save the whole mankind.

00:32:53.970 --> 00:32:59.300
If so, how can the unsaved people be saved, if that's possible at all?

00:32:59.680 --> 00:33:01.260
There's no answer.

00:33:01.680 --> 00:33:06.520
But, if you could open the Vortex and terminate the world,

00:33:07.150 --> 00:33:11.190
you could record all deaths up until the end of the world and examine them.

00:33:11.320 --> 00:33:16.700
If you could re-examine all that were unrewarded or unsaved in the new light,

00:33:17.240 --> 00:33:21.370
those who died meaningless deaths could then be exonerated.

00:33:21.870 --> 00:33:25.710
You'd be able to determine what their happiness was.

00:33:26.460 --> 00:33:28.960
What in the world are you?

00:33:30.460 --> 00:33:32.750
I'm no one.

00:33:33.260 --> 00:33:35.470
I just want a conclusion...

00:33:36.010 --> 00:33:40.720
that the filth of those ignorant humans is

00:33:41.390 --> 00:33:46.230
what will be recorded in history

00:33:46.480 --> 00:33:49.900
after they're long gone.

00:33:49.980 --> 00:33:52.230
That would help me feel at peace.

00:33:52.570 --> 00:33:58.240
You want to eradicate foul humans for your own sake.

00:33:58.820 --> 00:34:03.740
But I was interrupted just a step away from succeeding.

00:34:04.080 --> 00:34:08.580
What poor losers! Humans don't know when to give up.

00:34:08.750 --> 00:34:13.050
It was an unexpected event that Tomoe Enjou had escaped this spiral.

00:34:13.130 --> 00:34:18.010
You had put up a civilization bound field to shield the view of the Deterrent Force.

00:34:18.090 --> 00:34:21.140
The field already had too many holes at that stage.

00:34:21.600 --> 00:34:25.470
You were defeated by Tomoe, a single person who represents family love.

00:34:27.850 --> 00:34:31.190
Let me tell you something.

00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:35.940
A psychologist has defined what's called the mass unconsciousness.

00:34:36.440 --> 00:34:41.200
It suggests that the bottom of human consciousness all leads to the same well.

00:34:41.450 --> 00:34:44.200
It's where all the egoism of the entire world is supposedly stored.

00:34:44.660 --> 00:34:48.710
It's called Araya-shiki in Buddhism.

00:34:49.210 --> 00:34:50.870
What?

00:34:51.130 --> 00:34:54.040
What an ironic paradox of the world.

00:34:54.960 --> 00:34:58.510
Your name and the name of the one you despise make up a profound word.

00:35:02.260 --> 00:35:06.310
This body has reached its limit.

00:35:07.230 --> 00:35:09.180
Start from scratch, then?

00:35:10.650 --> 00:35:14.900
I don't have a spare body.

00:35:22.620 --> 00:35:23.530
Araya.

00:35:23.990 --> 00:35:25.490
What do you seek?

00:35:25.740 --> 00:35:27.870
True wisdom.

00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:30.710
Araya, where do you seek it?

00:35:31.000 --> 00:35:34.250
Only within myself.

00:35:34.670 --> 00:35:37.590
Araya, to where are you headed?

00:35:38.170 --> 00:35:42.550
Of course... the end of the spiral...

00:35:42.760 --> 00:35:46.810
of this paradox world.

00:36:28.060 --> 00:36:31.890
You have the ability to record your memories like a film,

00:36:32.100 --> 00:36:34.730
so why is it that you're also able to forget them?

00:36:36.110 --> 00:36:38.400
You couldn't help forgetting?

00:36:38.770 --> 00:36:39.940
No...

00:36:40.440 --> 00:36:43.150
It's just a matter of not recalling.

00:36:44.240 --> 00:36:46.490
I'm sure that you remember...

00:36:47.580 --> 00:36:50.410
Unlike me, lacking the ability to record,

00:36:50.580 --> 00:36:53.960
the memories of human beings can never be lost.

00:36:56.420 --> 00:37:00.210
To forget something is to drive it into obsolescence.

00:37:01.130 --> 00:37:03.720
Memories are never lost...

00:37:03.930 --> 00:37:06.090
Rather, they are debris that fade away with time.

00:37:07.050 --> 00:37:09.430
Don't you find that a waste?

00:37:10.470 --> 00:37:13.930
To let all that is eternal rust away.

00:37:14.850 --> 00:37:17.770
To take what is eternal...

00:37:17.900 --> 00:37:20.900
...and turn it into so much settling dust with your own hands.

00:37:22.610 --> 00:37:27.280
The fact that it's not eternal means that it is eternal.

00:37:28.660 --> 00:37:31.450
Eternity must be returned.

00:37:31.620 --> 00:37:34.040
And I shall play back the grief that results from it.

00:37:34.830 --> 00:37:37.460
Even if you happen to forget it.

00:37:38.880 --> 00:37:43.000
Because without a doubt, it's been recorded inside you.

00:37:45.170 --> 00:37:47.630
Who decides what is eternal?

00:37:49.140 --> 00:37:51.140
Even I don't know the answer to that.

00:37:52.100 --> 00:37:55.020
That's what I've been searching for all this time.

00:38:03.360 --> 00:38:06.990
You do things in a roundabout way, don't you?

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:08.200
What's your goal?

00:38:08.320 --> 00:38:12.830
I don't know. I simply granted someone else's wish.

00:38:13.120 --> 00:38:17.000
This is happening all because of those girls' wishes.

00:38:17.330 --> 00:38:20.210
I don't have a goal of my own, but...

00:38:20.750 --> 00:38:22.500
...this must be fate.

00:38:22.840 --> 00:38:27.510
I came to this country at Souren Araya's request...

00:38:27.680 --> 00:38:32.140
...to return the memories you lost to the oblivion two years ago.

00:38:32.510 --> 00:38:36.770
No, you, too, are looking for your lost memories.

00:38:37.230 --> 00:38:41.350
I can see your mind hidden in your words.

00:38:42.270 --> 00:38:44.980
That is my only duty.

00:38:46.440 --> 00:38:48.860
Are you a magus, too?

00:38:49.780 --> 00:38:53.530
Yes. I'm a magus who controls words.

00:38:53.700 --> 00:38:56.240
I'm called Godot Word.

00:39:01.040 --> 00:39:04.380
I am unable to reaffirm what I have witnessed.

00:39:05.380 --> 00:39:07.550
Whatever knowledge I've gained beyond what I've seen...

00:39:07.630 --> 00:39:10.880
...is not a memory, it's no more than information.

00:39:12.390 --> 00:39:14.470
The world is not a film.

00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:18.310
Rather, it has been replaced by words, becoming mere information.

00:39:19.140 --> 00:39:20.310
And my...

00:39:20.770 --> 00:39:21.730
No...

00:39:22.360 --> 00:39:27.730
The world outside me has been frozen in time from the time I was ten.

00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:38.540
Oblivion Recording
January, 1999

00:39:49.090 --> 00:39:51.260
What's going on, Miss Touko?

00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:55.800
Ah! Sounds like the secret weapon has arrived safely.

00:39:56.260 --> 00:39:59.770
I have orders from Miss Touko Aozaki to be here.

00:40:10.360 --> 00:40:15.160
An object only acquires meaning when it has an observer.

00:40:16.660 --> 00:40:19.950
Therefore, even if the object itself is unchanging,

00:40:20.120 --> 00:40:23.460
if the observer gets the impression that it is variable,

00:40:23.580 --> 00:40:25.790
then it cannot be considered eternal.

00:40:27.550 --> 00:40:30.050
New objects eventually grow old,

00:40:30.300 --> 00:40:32.800
and magnificent objects end up fading.

00:40:33.970 --> 00:40:36.720
Even though the object itself may not change,

00:40:37.140 --> 00:40:41.810
our own minds cause its value to change.

00:40:44.060 --> 00:40:45.810
The fairies are coming!

00:40:53.150 --> 00:40:55.410
That's fantastic.

00:41:02.500 --> 00:41:06.170
The fairies can take only the memories that you remember.

00:41:06.420 --> 00:41:11.340
No one can collect lost memories... the oblivion.

00:41:13.920 --> 00:41:18.180
I have no recollection of the very moment

00:41:18.260 --> 00:41:20.810
I fell in love with Mikiya.

00:41:22.520 --> 00:41:25.560
He controls people's recognition using words,

00:41:25.690 --> 00:41:28.270
but he has no other means to attack.

00:41:31.440 --> 00:41:32.650
There's nothing in that direction.

00:41:32.740 --> 00:41:34.860
I'm in a hurry. So, if you'll excuse me...

00:41:37.700 --> 00:41:38.490
Shiki,

00:41:39.530 --> 00:41:41.530
To be eternal...

00:41:41.870 --> 00:41:44.410
...means not having a shape.

00:41:49.380 --> 00:41:52.550
Good... very good...

00:41:52.760 --> 00:41:54.210
Miss Kokutou!

00:41:56.430 --> 00:41:58.220
I am nobody special.

00:41:59.550 --> 00:42:02.060
All I want is a way to resolve this.

00:42:03.720 --> 00:42:05.770
I've never laughed in my life.

00:42:06.890 --> 00:42:07.810
Not once.

00:42:09.900 --> 00:42:12.230
You will lose sight of where you're going.

00:42:18.990 --> 00:42:21.410
I shall replay the grief,

00:42:21.740 --> 00:42:23.830
even though you've totally forgot it.

00:42:23.910 --> 00:42:27.710
...because the memory is vividly recorded inside you.

00:42:41.470 --> 00:42:42.800
Out of my way!

00:42:56.690 --> 00:43:02.570
Don't underestimate me!

00:43:05.370 --> 00:43:07.290
Die already!

00:43:22.600 --> 00:43:24.050
Is it over?

00:43:26.640 --> 00:43:28.020
Sure thing!

00:43:44.330 --> 00:43:45.910
Azaka, what about the bus?

00:43:46.700 --> 00:43:48.490
It's freezing cold!

00:43:52.500 --> 00:43:55.590
Brother, I'm starved!

00:44:18.650 --> 00:44:20.940
I had a dream about our childhood.

00:44:22.570 --> 00:44:26.120
Someone who was close and important to my brother and me

00:44:26.200 --> 00:44:27.240
passed away.

00:44:29.330 --> 00:44:36.250
He looked very sad but he never shed tears.

00:44:41.050 --> 00:44:43.470
He is normal to the maximum and he is the last person

00:44:43.550 --> 00:44:44.970
to hurt anyone else.

00:44:45.300 --> 00:44:49.260
He can understand everyone but no one notices him.

00:44:49.390 --> 00:44:51.060
What an empty loneliness...

00:44:54.140 --> 00:44:55.350
At that moment...

00:44:55.850 --> 00:45:00.150
I think Mikiya Kokutou became someone precious to me,

00:45:00.690 --> 00:45:04.650
someone I should never lose at any cost.

00:45:08.580 --> 00:45:12.660
Since you have the ability to forget so easily, I'm sure you wouldn't understand.

00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:19.000
The only thing that can be called eternal in this world is the human memory.

00:45:20.630 --> 00:45:25.010
Your misconception is that memories are created when your life is over.

00:45:25.550 --> 00:45:26.880
The truth is...

00:45:27.140 --> 00:45:31.260
That your life is added on only after all of your memories are created.

00:45:32.600 --> 00:45:35.730
There are no memories that should be forgotten.

00:45:36.440 --> 00:45:38.940
As for memories discarded by the personality,

00:45:39.020 --> 00:45:41.650
it was the owner of those memories that wanted to be rid of them.

00:45:43.030 --> 00:45:46.400
And that's why whatever you wish for...

00:45:46.990 --> 00:45:49.490
...is never anything more than an oblivion recording.

00:48:29.110 --> 00:48:31.400
I really like you.

00:48:32.070 --> 00:48:33.610
So I'll see you again very soon.

00:48:37.620 --> 00:48:39.290
The strawberry Häagen-Dazs.

00:48:39.620 --> 00:48:42.870
Your carton's still in the freezer. Knock it back before you go.

00:48:42.960 --> 00:48:45.120
Knock it back - are you serious?

00:48:45.330 --> 00:48:48.210
You've got to do something about that mouth of yours, at least.

00:48:48.880 --> 00:48:50.960
You're a girl, after all.

00:49:59.870 --> 00:50:01.280
I knew...

00:50:03.250 --> 00:50:07.580
I knew that you were the only one waiting for me

00:50:09.040 --> 00:50:14.670
and you were the only one protecting me...

00:50:18.390 --> 00:50:19.840
Just a little...

00:50:19.930 --> 00:50:24.560
A little murderous impulse toward you...

00:50:31.570 --> 00:50:34.070
Everything in this world has a tear.

00:50:34.440 --> 00:50:36.190
Not to mention humans,

00:50:36.400 --> 00:50:40.030
the atmosphere, one's will and even time.

00:50:40.660 --> 00:50:43.700
My eyes allow me to see death.

00:50:45.500 --> 00:50:46.580
So,

00:50:47.660 --> 00:50:49.290
I can kill even a god

00:50:50.170 --> 00:50:51.830
if he lives...

00:50:52.250 --> 00:50:55.300
I've seen the secret of your magic!

00:50:56.380 --> 00:50:58.010
Stop making excuses.

00:50:59.220 --> 00:51:00.720
Good, Asagami... You are the best.

00:51:02.100 --> 00:51:04.560
You should decided that one.

00:53:13.350 --> 00:53:14.480
Good evening.

00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:40.380
April of 1995...

00:53:41.460 --> 00:53:44.300
I met her.

01:00:20.990 --> 01:00:23.490
<b>Next Episode</b>

01:00:25.830 --> 01:00:26.830
Who...

01:00:26.990 --> 01:00:28.830
...is going to kill who?

01:00:28.950 --> 01:00:33.830
I need her, Ryougi the murderer.

01:00:34.330 --> 01:00:40.880
But... because of you, Ryougi won't come to my world.

01:00:43.890 --> 01:00:50.970
Back then, I chose to stay with her, instead of going home alone.

01:00:52.020 --> 01:00:53.730
Three years after the night SHIKI vanished...

01:00:54.020 --> 01:00:56.860
Shiki, don't! Come back!

01:00:57.860 --> 01:01:00.530
You shouldn't kill him.

01:01:00.690 --> 01:01:02.360
I shouldn't kill?

01:01:03.240 --> 01:01:05.160
None of your business.

01:01:05.780 --> 01:01:11.580
Shiki. If you kill Rio, I won't forgive you.

01:01:15.330 --> 01:01:19.540
Murder Speculation (Part B)
